Frequently Asked Questions

Q: Can I self-host ZWarden to manage my PZ servers?
A: Yes. Always. That is the primary intended use.

Q: Can I modify the source code for my own deployment?
A: Yes.

Q: Can I run ZWarden for my gaming community or clan?
A: Yes. Managing your own servers for your community is permitted use.

Q: What is NOT allowed?
A: Offering ZWarden (or a modified version) as a hosted service to third
   parties — i.e., running a commercial "ZWarden-as-a-Service" platform
   where other people sign up and you manage their PZ servers using this
   software. If you want to do that, contact the Licensor for a commercial
   license.

Q: What happens on the Change Date?
A: This version of the code automatically becomes available under the
   Apache License 2.0, a permissive open-source license with no
   restrictions on commercial use.
